bug_report:
[7/8/9 Regression] incorrect "invalid use of incomplete type" in a lambda on valid code
This valid code:

template<class T>
class A {
    static A* INSTANCE;
    void foobar();
    void moo() {}
};

template<class T>
A<T>* A<T>::INSTANCE = nullptr;

template<class T>
void A<T>::foobar() {
    auto x = []() {
        INSTANCE->moo();
    };
}

(compiled with -Wall)

Gives error:
<source>: In lambda function:

<source>:14:17: error: invalid use of incomplete type 'class A<T>' [-Werror]

         INSTANCE->moo();

This compiles fine with Clang and GCC 6, but fails with the error above with GCC 7 and 8.
